  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 154 PM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nThe unseasonable heat will extend into at least Thursday. Heat \nadvisories have been continued into Thursday and may be necessary\nfor some areas Friday into the weekend. The confidence is much\nlower for the weekend on their necessity, however, with lower dew\npoints expected for Saturday. A cold front will approach and move\nthrough the area late in the weekend, bringing substantially\ncooler conditions to the region extending into the early part of\nthe next week. The front will also bring increased chances for\nshowers and thunderstorms, particularly for the latter part of the\nweekend and into early next week. There is some uncertainty\nregarding the timing of all of this, with recent data pushed about\na day later than earlier expectations. In addition to the much\nwelcomed expectation of cooler and wetter conditions, however, is\nan increase in the fire weather concerns for Saturday, in advance\nof this system. Southerly winds will become gusty ahead of the\nfront, and along with the continued warm conditions and\naforementioned lower dew points, very low relative humidities are\nforecast. This combination, along with the drought-stricken fuels,\nwill lead to the fire weather concerns, especially across\nsoutheast Oklahoma, on Saturday. Given the information we have at\nthe moment and coordination with fire management agencies, this \nmay be a Fire Danger Statement day rather than something stronger.",
